<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aishwarya of Nepal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1949">1949</a>–<a href="/years/2001">2001</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Queen Aishwarya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aishwarya (1949–2001) was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> as the wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birendra-of-nepal">King Birendra</a>, whom she married in 1970. A member of the Rana family, she was regarded as an influential figure at court and wrote poetry under a pen name. She was killed with her husband and other members of the royal family in the massacre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narayanhiti-palace">Narayanhiti Palace</a> on 1 June 2001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aishwarya-of-nepal.jpg" alt="Aishwarya of Nepal" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aishwarya_1972.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
